.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-DELETE-EGRESS-LIMIT 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-delete-egress-limit \- remove an application's egress limit for an outside site
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eap delete-egress-limit
\fB\-\-application\-id\fR \fIid\fR
\fB\-\-site\fR \fIhost\fR|\fB*\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a limit set with
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1).
For a site, the application is then held to its
.I *
default for that site, or to
.I euclid.modules.eap.egress.default
if it has none. With
.BR "\-\-site '*'" ,
the application's default is removed, and its sites without a limit of
their own fall back to
.IR euclid.modules.eap.egress.default .
.PP
What's in flight to the site, and a block it asked for, stay counted:
forgetting them would let the site be overrun the moment this is run.
Fails with HTTP 404 if there's no such limit. The caller must be an
administrator.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-application\-id " " \fIid\fR
The application the limit is for.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-site " " \fIhost\fR|\fB*\fR
The site's host name, or \fB*\fR for the application's default.
.SH OUTPUT
The application, the site and the limits now in force for it, as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap delete-egress-limit --application-id downloader --site downloads.example.com
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-list-egress-sites (1)
